.TH WAVE-BASEDIR 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-basedir \- Print MacWave's install root -- the base_dir in config.json, which is where the binaries, the links and the dependencies live. A path under your home directory is shown with ~. With --raw it prints the absolute path as-is and nothing else.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave basedir [\-\-raw]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print MacWave's install root -- the base_dir in config.json, which is
where the binaries, the links and the dependencies live. A path under
your home directory is shown with ~. With --raw it prints the absolute
path as-is and nothing else.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the absolute path as-is, with no emoji or colour (for scripts)

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave basedir
wave basedir --raw
cd "$(wave basedir --raw)"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
